===== final-1.txt
I wrote no plan for add-greeting, because its spec hasn't been approved.

`changes/add-greeting/spec.md` has no `approved:` line, and I'm not allowed to plan an unapproved spec. Its header lists size, owner, repos and supersedes, but nothing records demo-owner's approval.

This isn't the case where a requirement is missing a scenario: R1 has R1.S1 and R1.S2, and R2 has R2.S1. Approval is the only thing missing.

I left the spec, code and tests alone. There is no `plan.md`, so the librarian has nothing to file and there are no `DESK:` git lines to print.

To unblock this, demo-owner needs to approve the spec, the spec author then adds the `approved:` line, and you can send the change back for planning.
